# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Donor and patient identifiers. Never commit these.
#
# The AMSC data is individual-level and stays in its protected environment. The
# code in this repository refers to donors only through placeholders such as
# <DONOR_ID> and through column names such as Patient_ID; no identifier values
# belong in any tracked file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*PRIVATE*
*private_donor*
V2F_PRIVATE_donor_ids.md
*donor_ids*
*donor_metadata*
*village_metadata*
AMSC_ids*
MOVE_ids*
*id_map*
*SUBJID*
*CGBID*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Individual-level inputs and MOVE working directories.
#
# These live in the protected environment where the notebooks are run. The
# paths are listed here so that a stray local copy can never be committed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Anchored to the repository root so that configs/MOVE/data/ stays tracked.
/data/
/data_residualized/
/interim_data/
/interim_data_rsd/
/interim_data_rsd_test/
/results_cont_paper*/
/results_temp/
/results_tune_model/
/synthetic_data*/
*.h5ad
*.h5
*.loom
*.mtx.gz

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Large or access-controlled source data
#
# DIAMANTE is behind an access form and the full file is ~700 MB. The 1000
# Genomes slices and PLINK binaries are all regenerable by the notebook.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.sumstat.txt
*.vcf.gz
*.vcf.gz.tbi
scripts/2_colocalization_and_finemapping/dat/raw/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Analysis inputs and outputs. The data folders each stage reads from, and
# everything under interim/ and results/, which the notebook or script that
# wrote it regenerates. The code is what this repository keeps; the YAML under
# configs/MOVE/data/ is configuration and stays tracked.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
scripts/**/dat/
scripts/**/data/
scripts/**/auxilliary_files/
**/interim/
**/results/
**/signed_ld/
*.nosex
*.dupvar

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Work that is not part of the manuscript: the sequence-to-function notebooks
# the combined AlphaGenome_Borzoi one replaced, and the analyses run on the
# later data release.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
scripts/3_sequence_to_function_modeling/scratch/
scripts/5_extra_analyses/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Everything that is not this project's own code. What the repository tracks
# is scripts/, configs/ and this Readme; the rest is either a copy of someone
# else's package, a browser-ready export, superseded output, or an archive of
# the tracked files themselves.
#
#   CARMA/, SharePro_coloc/   local copies of both packages, upstream elsewhere
#   UWash_tracks/             ChromBPNet tracks exported for the WashU browser
#   archive_unsigned/         results from before the LD matrix carried a sign
#   paper/                    the manuscript
#   scripts.zip               a zip of scripts/
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/CARMA/
/SharePro_coloc/
/UWash_tracks/
/archive_unsigned/
/paper/
/scripts.zip

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# R
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.RData
.Rhistory
.Rapp.history
.Rproj.user/
*.Rproj

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Jupyter and Python
#
# Notebook outputs are stripped before committing; see the Reproducibility
# section of Readme.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.ipynb_checkpoints/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.virtual_documents/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# API keys and other local secrets.
#
# The AlphaGenome notebook reads ALPHA_GENOME_API_KEY from .env, which VS Code
# also loads into the kernel's environment. No .env variant is ever committed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Downloads the sequence-model notebook makes for itself: a cached slice of
# hg38 and the Borzoi track annotation, both re-fetched on demand.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
sequence_cache/
targets_human.txt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# macOS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
